snp2.12:3.4 | S: energetic, a resolute Seer of Truth. | T: with persistence aroused.
snp2.12:4.1 | S: O Sakyan, All-seer, | T: Sakyan, All-around Eye,
snp2.12:4.2 | S: we all wish to know about that disciple. | T: we all, too, want to know of that disciple:
snp2.12:4.3 | S: Our ears are eager to hear, | T: Ready to hear are our ears.
snp2.12:4.4 | S: for you are the most excellent teacher. | T: You, our teacher: You are unexcelled.
snp2.12:5.1 | S: Cut off our doubt, declare this to us; | T: Cut through our uncertainty. Tell me this,
snp2.12:5.2 | S: your wisdom is vast, tell us of his quenching! | T: make known, One of discernment deep, that he was totally unbound.
snp2.12:5.3 | S: All-seer, speak among us, | T: Like Thousand-eyed Sakka, in the midst of the devas, speak, All-around Eye, in ours.
snp2.12:5.4 | S: like the thousand-eyed Sakka <j>in the midst of the gods! | T: (none)
snp2.12:6.1 | S: Whatever ties there are, or paths to delusion, | T: Here, whatever snares there are, paths of delusion,
