snp2.12:7.4 | S: not even brilliant men would shine. | T: Even brilliant people wouldn’t shine bright.
snp2.12:8.1 | S: The attentive are bringers of light; | T: But the enlightened are makers of light.
snp2.12:8.2 | S: my hero, that is what I think of you. | T: Thus I think you’re that, enlightened one.
snp2.12:8.3 | S: We’ve come for your discernment and knowledge: | T: We have come to one who knows through clear-seeing.
snp2.12:8.4 | S: here in this assembly, declare to us about Kappāyana. | T: Make Kappa shine in our assembly.
snp2.12:9.1 | S: Swiftly send forth your sweet, sweet voice, | T: Quickly, handsome one, stir your handsome voice.
snp2.12:9.2 | S: like a goose stretching its neck, gently honking, | T: Like a swan, stretching out (its neck), call gently
snp2.12:9.3 | S: lucid-flowing, with lovely tone: | T: with rounded tones, well-modulated.
snp2.12:9.4 | S: alert, we all listen to you. | T: We all listen to you, sitting upright.
snp2.12:10.1 | S: You have entirely abandoned birth and death; | T: Pleading, I shall get the pure one to speak, he whose birth & death are abandoned.
snp2.12:10.2 | S: curbed and pure, I urge you, speak the Dhamma! | T: (none)
