snp2.12:12.3 | S: As a man baking in the summer sun <j>would long for water, | T: I long for the water of your speech as if distressed in mind by the heat in the summer.
snp2.12:12.4 | S: I long for your voice, so let the sound rain  forth. | T: Rain down a torrent.
snp2.12:13.1 | S: Surely Kappāyana did not <j>lead the spiritual life in vain? | T: Was the holy life, as led by Kappa in line with his aim? Was it not in any way in vain?
